# vim:tw=80:ft=pnlc:
# inc:../prelude.pnlc

# in 1999 David Madore accidentally stumbled upon the Unlambda program
#     ``r`ci`.*`ci
# in Scheme one would write
#     (((lambda (cc) (newline)        cc) (call/cc (lambda (cc) cc)))
#      ((lambda (cc) (write-char #\*) cc) (call/cc (lambda (cc) cc))))
# each line of output is a string of asterisks, the `n`th line consisting
# of `n` asterisks. what follows is a translation of the program to PNLC.
# it's much noisier because we have to use the continuation monad to reify
# continuations

.main ..join io:mnad ...apply io:aptv
  ...bind io:mnad .callcc .pure io:aptv \cc ...fmapk io:ftor cc .putc '\n'
  ...bind io:mnad .callcc .pure io:aptv \cc ...fmapk io:ftor cc .putc '*'
